src/cellpose.js ports the Cellpose 3.1.1.1 inference, tiling and mask
reconstruction pipeline (https://github.com/MouseLand/cellpose: normalize99,
get_pad_yx, make_tiles, average_tiles, _taper_mask, run_net, run_3D,
follow_flows, steps_interp, map_coordinates, get_masks_torch,
masks_to_flows_cpu, flow_error, remove_bad_flow_masks,
fill_holes_and_remove_small_masks). Cellpose is Copyright (c) 2020-2025,
Howard Hughes Medical Institute, authored by Carsen Stringer and Marius
Pachitariu, under the BSD 3-Clause licence (LICENSE).

The ONNX models (cellpose-cyto3.onnx and cellpose-nuclei.onnx) are converted
from Cellpose's pretrained cyto3 and nucleitorch_0 weights
(https://www.cellpose.org/models/cyto3 and
https://www.cellpose.org/models/nucleitorch_0) by validation/export_model.py.
While the Cellpose codebase is BSD-3-Clause, several training datasets used to
train the pretrained Cellpose weights (including the Cellpose training set and
TissueNet) are licensed under CC-BY-NC (Attribution-NonCommercial); commercial
deployments should train models on commercially permissible data.

Stringer C, Wang T, Michaelos M, Pachitariu M (2021). Cellpose: a generalist
algorithm for cellular segmentation. Nature Methods 18(1):100-106.

Stringer C, Pachitariu M (2025). Cellpose3: one-click image restoration for
improved segmentation. Nature Methods 22:592-599.
